  "summary": "Ardmore, Oklahoma city commissioners voted 3-1 to renew the city's Flock license plate reader contract, sparking a recall petition targeting the three commissioners who voted yes plus one who was absent. Petition organizers say commissioners cut off discussion and blocked public input on privacy concerns; the acting city manager said Oklahoma's Open Meetings Act does not require public comment.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The biggest beef is that they didn't allow any of the citizens to really express opposition to these cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "It doesn't matter what my position about Flock is \u2014 whether I love it or hate it \u2014 it's what my constituents want",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "These meetings are strictly business meetings to do the city's business in an open forum",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
